From 00a6a7a4c28fb9a307a9445ce6fa967545f812b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:27:04 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] project: revive three upstream git tests that were ignored
 and had rotted

Three integration tests in crates/project/tests/integration/project_tests.rs
were `#[ignore]`d upstream and, run with --run-ignored on 2026-10-09, failed:
nobody runs an ignored test, so upstream's changes to git_store kept moving
under them. None of the failures came from this series -- no patch touches
worktree, git or fs code -- but an ignored test covers nothing, and two of
these pin a real property: changes inside a gitignored directory (a cargo
flycheck writing into target/) must not emit RepositoryUpdated events.

  test_git_status_postprocessing -- upstream now computes `diff_stat` for a
  combined `DA` status too. HEAD and the working copy are both empty, so the
  expected stat is Some(0/0), not None.

  test_ignored_dirs_events, test_odd_events_for_ignored_dirs -- both pinned
  the exact list of events the initial scan emits ([StatusesChanged], and
  [HeadChanged, StatusesChanged, StatusesChanged]); today's scan emits
  [HeadChanged, BranchListChanged] and [HeadChanged]. That list is what made
  them flaky in the first place (upstream's own todo: "susceptible to
  different timings/ordering of events"), and it is not what they test. The
  initial check now asserts the scan reported the repository (HeadChanged is
  present); every assertion after the ignored-directory changes stays exact.

All three are un-ignored. Measured: 20/20 iterations under
`cargo nextest run --stress-count 20`, and green in the full 30-crate suite.

Tests only; nothing here is compiled into the editor. Unconditional, like
every test the series carries.
---

